{"raw": {"https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Clinical-Professor-of-Nursing_JR100681": {"title": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking two qualified applicants for Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing positions. The standard teaching load is 12 course credit hours per semester or 24 credits over an academic year. This position seeks candidates with at least two years of medical-surgical and/or critical care nursing expertise. Experience in critical care settings, such as ICU, Emergency Department, or Telemetry, is highly preferred. This position carries ongoing responsibility for curriculum development, planning, teaching, guiding, monitoring, and evaluating student learning in the classroom and clinical practice settings to support continuous improvement of courses and clinical experiences. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Willi ngness \u00a0 to teach \u00a0 across nursing programs \u00a0 based on departmental needs . \u00a0 Teaching theor y, laboratory, and /or \u00a0 clinical \u00a0 components \u00a0 in nursing education program s . \u00a0 Teaching \u00a0 and evaluating assigned courses.\u00a0 \u00a0 Supervising student performance of clinical skills in the lab and/or clinical setting s ( clinical faculty -to- student ratio is not more than 1:10 ) . \u00a0 Promot ing \u00a0 positive and productive relationships with service are a \u00a0 hospitals, clinics, and agencies . \u00a0 Participat ing \u00a0 in \u00a0 program, department, and university \u00a0 assessment \u00a0 and accreditation \u00a0 activities. \u00a0 \u00a0 Participat ing \u00a0 in academic advising and guidance of students \u00a0 Attend ing \u00a0 p rogram and \u00a0 d epartment faculty meetings.\u00a0 \u00a0 Providing students \u00a0 with \u00a0 a \u00a0 detailed course \u00a0 syllabus \u00a0 in writing, \u00a0 following CMU \u00a0 Nursing guidelines \u00a0 and timelines . \u00a0 Establishing, posting, and keeping a minimum of five office hours weekly over four days during each term of the academic year.\u00a0 \u00a0 Establishing \u00a0 necessary \u00a0 procedures to \u00a0 ensure \u00a0 that adequate and \u00a0 accurate \u00a0 records of student performance are \u00a0 maintained . \u00a0 Developing and \u00a0 maintaining : \u00a0 An active scholarship \u00a0 portfolio \u00a0 ( for t enure-track Assistant Professor), or \u00a0 Ongoing professional productivity and clinical \u00a0 expertise \u00a0 (Assistant Clinical Professor) \u00a0 Provid ing \u00a0 service to the \u00a0 program, department, \u00a0 university , \u00a0 and external community.\u00a0 \u00a0 Participat ing \u00a0 in program, department, and university events including commencement. \u00a0 Maintaining \u00a0 t imely \u00a0 and satisfactory performance of responsibilities specified in the faculty member\u2019s employment agreement and CMU Professional Employee Handbook.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u200b Salary: $60,000-$70,000 (master\u2019s prepared); $70,000-$80,000 (doctoral prepared) Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! EDUCATION \u00a0 AND \u00a0 EXPERIENCE: \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Required \u00a0 Qualifications \u00a0 E ligible for or hold ing \u00a0 a current license in \u00a0 good standing \u00a0 to practice as a Registered Nurse in Colorado .\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Minimum of \u00a0 two years of \u00a0 full-time \u00a0 professional clinical \u00a0 nursing \u00a0 experience , with preference given to candidates with experience in critical care settings (ICU, ED, Telemetry) \u00a0 \u00a0 Graduate degree in \u00a0 n ursing \u00a0 from a \u00a0 national accredited school of nursing.\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrate knowledge and skills related to : \u00a0 Adult learning principles \u00a0 Teaching \u00a0 methodology \u00a0 C urriculum development and evaluation \u00a0 O r a written plan for obtaining such knowledge \u00a0 beginning no later than the first year of teaching. \u00a0 \u00a0 LANGUAGE SKILLS \u00a0 Ability to read, analyze, and interpret \u00a0 professional journals, technical procedures, and governmental regulations. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from \u00a0 students, colleagues, and community partners.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 MATHEMATICAL SKILLS \u00a0 Ability to apply basic mathematical concepts such as fractions, percentages, \u00a0 ratios \u00a0 and proportions to practic e \u00a0 situations. \u00a0 \u00a0 REASONING ABILITY \u00a0 Ability to define problems, collect \u00a0 and analyze \u00a0 data, \u00a0 establish \u00a0 facts, and draw valid conclusions. \u00a0 \u00a0 PHYSICAL DEMANDS \u00a0 The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable \u00a0 accommodation \u00a0 may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00a0 While performing the duties of this job, the employee is \u00a0 frequently \u00a0 required to stand, walk, sit, and talk, or hear. The employee must occasionally lift and/move up to 10 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include clos e, \u00a0 distance \u00a0 and \u00a0 peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust \u00a0 focus . \u00a0 \u00a0 WORK ENVIRONMENT \u00a0 The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable \u00a0 accommodation \u00a0 may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in office, classroom, and clinical settings. The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day. \u00a0 \u00a0 DEADLINE : \u00a0 To ensure consideration, complete applications should be received \u00a0 by \u00a0October 15, 2026. DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Jodi Noga, jnoga@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:\u00a0 Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100682": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Medical Office Assisting", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: CMU Tech\u2019s Allied Health Program is seeking 2 enthusiastic Adjunct Instructors to teach in our Medical Assistant program, one in Montrose and one in Grand Junction. This flexible position is ideal for experienced healthcare professionals\u2014including Medical Assistants, Pharmacy Technicians, Medical Coders/Billers, Medical Administrative Professionals, Nurses, EMTs/Paramedics\u2014who are passionate about preparing students for rewarding careers in healthcare. Courses may be delivered in a hybrid format, combining online instruction with occasional hands-on skills labs that may be supported by CMU Tech\u2019s high-tech Mobile Learning Lab. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Include but are not limited to: \u00a0 Instructional Responsibilities: \u00a0 Teach one or more Medical Assistant courses (e.g., administrative procedures, clinical skills, coding/billing, EHR, pharmacology, patient care). \u00a0 Deliver instruction aligned with approved syllabi, accreditation guidelines, and program standards. \u00a0 Incorporate real-world examples and skillsets that reflect current industry practices. \u00a0 Professional Development: \u00a0 Maintain relevant certifications and licensure. \u00a0 Integrate current industry standards and technologies into teaching practices. \u00a0 Use online learning platforms and tools to support student success. \u00a0 Student Support: \u00a0 Be available to students outside of class for questions and mentoring. \u00a0 Engage with students using a variety of tools (Zoom, email, phone, synchronous chats). \u00a0 Foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment. \u00a0 Commitment to Student Success: \u00a0 Emphasize hands-on, real-world skill development. \u00a0 Tailor \u00a0 instruction \u00a0 to meet diverse student learning needs. \u00a0 Encourage confidence, competence, and professionalism \u00a0 in \u00a0 all students. \u00a0 Support career readiness and \u00a0 credentialing \u00a0 preparation. \u00a0 Salary: $600.00 - $850.00 per credit hour. \u200c MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: \u00a0 Minimum of \u00a0 3 years \u00a0 of experience in a healthcare role such as \u00a0 Medical Assisting, Nursing, Pharmacy Technician, Coding & Billing, Medical Office Management, or EMT/Paramedic . \u00a0 Strong understanding of patient care, clinical workflows, or administrative healthcare systems. \u00a0 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: \u00a0 Previous \u00a0 teaching or training experience (formal or informal). \u00a0 National certification (e.g., RMA, CMA, \u00a0 CPhT , CPC, NCCT, etc.). \u00a0 Career and Technical Education (CTE) credential or willingness to obtain upon hire. \u00a0 DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Pam Holder, pholder@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:\u00a0 Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Sociology_JR100667": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Sociology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Social and Behavioral Sciences department at Colorado Mesa University is seeking an adjunct instructor of sociology. Colorado Mesa University is a state-funded, largely undergraduate institution that emphasizes quality teaching. The standard course in sociology at CMU is a 3-credit hour class. The instructor will teach one course to start, with the potential for future offerings. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching \u00a0introductory-level sociology courses such as\u00a0Marriage and Families, General Sociology, and/or Social Problems. \u00a0 Teaching in other areas of specialization within the sociology discipline will be considered, requisite with the candidate\u2019s experience and expertise. The ability to teach in-person lecture format, as well as online. The ability to teach quality courses including delivering course content, facilitating student discussions and activities, assessing student learning, and providing timely and responsive communication and feedback to students. Salary: $600.00 - $850.00 per credit hour. Adjunct faculty are paid on a per credit hour basis, commensurate with education and experience. \u200c Minimum Qualifications Required: Master\u2019s degree in Sociology. Experience teaching introductory-level sociology courses. Experience with basic classroom technology Preferred Qualifications: Candidates that can demonstrate excellence in teaching the required courses for this position will be given preference. Candidates with experience using the Desire 2 Learn (D2L) learning management system will be given preference. Candidates with strong communication skills and demonstrated responsiveness to students will be given preference. DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Megan Henley, mhenley@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:\u00a0 Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-Master-of-Science-in-Occupational-Therapy_JR100562": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor/Clinical Professor for Master of Science in Occupational Therapy", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor for the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program with practice mastery in physical rehabilitation. This is a full-time tenure-track or clinical-track, 12-month position with a start date of January 6, 2027. The standard academic load is 18-20 credit hours per year on site. Participation in scholarship, advising, and service to the program, department, and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach graduate-level courses within the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program. Develop and coordinate course design, course delivery, and participate in the evaluation of didactic and clinical curriculum. Advise and mentor graduate students, including guiding faculty-led research projects Initiate an ongoing scholarly agenda in area of expertise. Ongoing development and evaluation of curriculum to align with program goals and accreditation standards. Support admissions and applicant screening processes Complete professional development activities and service to the Department, University and community. Participate in ACOTE accreditation, and program/University assessment processes. Perform other program and department level duties as assigned. Salary: $95,000-$100,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty and responsibility satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.\u00a0 EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:\u00a0 Minimum Qualifications Required:\u00a0 EITHER A) Occupational therapist with the following: Master's degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program AND currently pursuing a Doctoral degree, or entry-level Doctoral degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. OR B) Post-professional OTD/DOT degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. All candidates should possess excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Detail-oriented with strong organizational, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience in adult physical rehabilitation. Previous academic teaching experience. Clinical teaching experience as a Level II Fieldwork educator. Evidence of scholarship (presentations, articles, posters, etc.). Active in community service and participation Leadership in local, regional, or national occupational therapy associations An earned terminal doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline (PhD, EdD). Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with adults in physical rehabilitation settings, working with students from diverse backgrounds, and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Deadline: This position will remain open until filled. Applications received by 9/15 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. How to Apply :\u00a0Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.\u00a0 In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.\u00a0 Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: Sarah Gray, search Chair at: sgray2@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Technical-Instructor-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100467": {"title": "Technical Instructor of Medical Office Assisting", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: We are seeking a passionate and experienced Medical Assistant Instructor to join our faculty. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in medical assisting and a dedication to teaching and mentoring students. As a Medical Assistant Instructor, you will be responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, developing curriculum, and ensuring that students acquire the skills and knowledge necessary to excel in the medical field. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct both lecture and lab instruction for 15 credit hours per semester and maintain 5 hours of office time per week for student consultation and support Work independently and collaboratively with colleagues to develop innovative curriculum that addresses the needs of our diverse student population. Demonstrate extensive knowledge and experience in medical assisting, utilizing the most current equipment and technology to enhance instruction in clinical and administrative procedures. Working knowledge and skill of up-to-date medical assisting principles, methods, and techniques. Evaluate student performance in coursework using industry-related standards and expectations to ensure competency and readiness for the workforce. Determine program needs and manage the program budget, including purchasing and cost control, to maintain high-quality educational resources. Maintain knowledge of industry-standard medical equipment and demonstrate its functionality in instructional settings. Engage successfully with students, healthcare professionals, other educators, and the public in a professional and courteous manner. Assist in the recruitment, advisement, placement, and development of cooperative work experience opportunities for students, and conduct follow-up with graduates. Serve as a representative of the department by participating in committees, task forces, and events at the campus, college, and/or state levels. Exhibit excellent organizational, communication, and presentation skills, along with a positive and enthusiastic attitude towards teaching and student success Excellent organization, communication, and presentation skills. Positive and enthusiastic attitude. Advise students, maintain student files and paperwork, including job sheets, registration, and intent to graduate. Coordinate industry engagement with local employers for advisory committee, internship, and other industry specific needs. Perform all responsibilities and instructional duties in accordance with local, state, and federal regulations as well as CMU Tech/CMU policies and procedures. Ensure the maintenance of appropriate approvals & accreditation, maintain and develop the curriculum in step with industry and state requirements. Promote a positive collegiate atmosphere and develop positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Applicant will perform other duties as required. Salary: $53,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.\u00a0 The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Minimum Qualifications Required: Minimum of 4,000 hours of w ork experience as a Medical Assistant in a clinical setting within the last five years. Preferred Qualifications: Associate degree or higher in related field Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) or Registered Medical Assistant (RMA) credentials. Evidence of teaching ability and or previous teaching experience in field COMPUTER SKILLS Ability to utilize PowerPoint, Learning Management System technology to maintain grades and content. LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures and governmental regulations.\u00a0 Ability to write reports, business correspondence and procedure manuals.\u00a0 Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, clients, customers and the public. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS Ability to apply accounting models and mathematical concepts such as probability and statistical inference.\u00a0 Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions to practical situations. REASONING ABILITY Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to interpret an extensive variety of technical instructions in mathematical or diagram form, to interpret an extensive variety of legal and regulatory documents and deal with several abstract and concrete variables. PHYSICAL DEMANDS\u00a0 The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, walk, sit, and talk or hear.\u00a0 The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 40 pounds.\u00a0 Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. WORK ENVIRONMENT\u00a0 The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in an open office setting.\u00a0 The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day. This position will remain open until\u00a0filled. Applications received by 9/1 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a weekly basis until the position is\u00a0filled. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Kinesiology_JR100111": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Kinesiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-22\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: CMU encourages students to engage in a healthy campus lifestyle. As part of our campus-wide Health and Wellness program, every student takes the Health & Wellness course and at least one activity class (and most take three or more) to meet graduation requirements for all undergraduate degrees. Our activity classes range from Aerobics to Zumba and we are always looking for local instructors who are highly experienced in the courses we offer. With the great community of health, fitness, and wellness experts we enjoy in Western Colorado, YOU could be a great fit to educate our Mavericks! Please explore the list below to see our full list of course offerings. If you see an activity you are trained in and passionate about, we encourage you to apply and join the Maverick family! List of Activity Courses: Beginning Swimming, Intermediate Swimming, Springboard Diving, Water Polo, Rock Climbing, Hiking, Beginning Golf, Intermediate Golf, Disc Golf and Ultimate Frisbee, Badminton, Karate, Beginning Tennis, Pickleball, Racquet Sports, Fitness Walking, Physical Conditioning, Intermediate Weight Training, Weight Training, Aerobics, Step Aerobics, Self-Defense, Pilates, Indoor Cycling, Adaptive Physical Activity, Introduction to Yoga, Hatha Yoga Relaxation, Flow Yoga, Zumba, Snorkeling/Free Diving, and Social Dance. In addition to our activity classes, we are also looking for instructors who may be interested and qualified to teach the Health & Wellness course. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching as an Adjunct Lecturer at CMU requires familiarity and use of our online learning platform, D2L, along with the ability to create a syllabus with engaging and educating methodologies to assess student learning.\u00a0 Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. \u200c Minimum Qualifications Required: Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher or we will consider accredited certification in your activity and/or 5 years of documented experienced teaching.\u00a0 Master's degree is required to teach KINE 100 Health and Wellness How to Apply :\u00a0Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.\u00a0 In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.\u00a0 Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: \u00a0Kristin Heumann, kheumann@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Lecturer-of-Business_JR100078": {"title": "Lecturer of Business", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-06\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking applications for a part-time in-person Lecturer of Economics. The ideal candidates would have experience teaching Economics principles courses. Part-time faculty at CMU are part-time employees who are hired on an as-needed basis. This job ad is to collect applications for qualified lecturers but communication to applicants may be delayed as faculty needs fluctuate. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. This position will consist of teaching one to two 3-credit hour courses per semester, starting fall 2026 (mid-August). Courses taught will be primarily the 200-level Principles of Microeconomics and/or Principles of Macroeconomics courses the first semester with options to teach upper-level economics courses in the future depending on experience. In addition, the Lecturer must hold a minimum of two office hours weekly for one course, plus a minimum of one office hour for each additional course, up to a maximum of five office hours per week. Salary: $600.00 - $850.00 per credit hour. Adjunct faculty are pair on a per credit hour basis, commensurate with education ad experience. \u200c Minimum Qualifications Required:\u00a0 Masters degree in Economics or closely-related discipline with at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Economics. Preferred Qualifications: PhD preferred but not required. How to Apply:\u00a0 Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: \u00a0Cover letter \u00a0Resume \u00a0Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for. Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.\u00a0 Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment. \u00a0Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) \u200b Direct Inquiries Contact: \u00a0Suzanne Owens-Ott; sowens@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Technical-Instructor-of-Electric-Lineworker_JR100709": {"title": "Technical Instructor of Electric Lineworker", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Do you have a passion for sharing your craft and teaching the next generation? If you have experience as an electric lineworker and a heart for students, we would love for you to join our family of exceptional instructors. The successful candidate will teach career and technical courses and perform administrative work at the CMU Tech Electric Lineworker Campus. This is an 11-month appointment. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach 15 credit hours per semester and maintain 5 hours of office hours per week.\u00a0 \u00a0 Work independently, as well as in collaboration with colleagues, to develop innovative curriculum which meets the needs of our diverse population of students.\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrate knowledge of, and experience in the field of electric lineworking, using the most current equipment, and other technology to enhance instruction in necessary areas. \u00a0 Working knowledge and skill of up-to-date industrial trade principles, methods, and techniques Determine program needs, maintain equipment, and maintain program budget The successful applicant will positively interact with students, business and industry representatives, other educators and educational institution representatives, and the public in a professional manner Assist in recruitment, advisement, placement, development of cooperative work experience opportunities for students and follow-up of students Serve as representative of the department by participating in committees, task forces, and events at the campus, college, and/or state levels Excellent organization, communication, and presentation skills. Positive and enthusiastic attitude Coordinate industry engagement with local employers for advisory committee, internship, and other industry specific needs Perform all responsibilities and instructional duties in accordance with local, state, and federal regulations as well as CMU/CMU Tech policies and procedures Ensure the maintenance of appropriate approvals & accreditation, maintain and develop the curriculum in step with industry and state requirements Other duties as required Salary: $85,000-$92,500 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: \u00a0 \u00a0 This position reports to the Director of Instruction. Position may require training and supervision of part-time instructors. \u00a0 \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS: \u00a0 \u00a0 To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.\u00a0 The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00a0 \u00a0 EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE \u00a0 \u00a0 REQUIRED: \u00a0 Certificate from an accredited institution in related field \u00a0 Minimum of 4,000 hours of experience in electric line working in the last 7 years. \u00a0 \u00a0 PREFERRED: \u00a0 Associates degree or higher in related field \u00a0 Supervisory experience \u00a0 Evidence of teaching ability and or previous teaching experience as a lineman \u00a0 COMPUTER SKILLS \u00a0 Ability to utilize PowerPoint, Learning Management System technology to maintain grades and content.\u00a0 \u00a0 LANGUAGE SKILLS \u00a0 \u00a0 Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures and governmental regulations.\u00a0 Ability to write reports, business correspondence and procedure manuals.\u00a0 Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, clients, customers and the public. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 MATHEMATICAL SKILLS \u00a0 \u00a0 Ability to apply accounting models and mathematical concepts such as probability and statistical inference.\u00a0 Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions to practical situations. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 REASONING ABILITY \u00a0 \u00a0 Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to interpret an extensive variety of technical instructions in mathematical or diagram form, to interpret an extensive variety of legal and regulatory documents and deal with several abstract and concrete variables. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 PHYSICAL DEMANDS\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, walk, sit, and talk or hear.\u00a0 The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 20 pounds.\u00a0 Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 WORK ENVIRONMENT\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in an open office setting.\u00a0 The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day. \u00a0 This position will remain open until \u00a0 filled . Applications received by 9/30 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is \u00a0 filled . How to Apply :\u00a0Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.\u00a0 In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.\u00a0 Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: Kelly Reuss, klreuss@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Geography_JR100717": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Geography", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Social and Behavioral Sciences department at Colorado Mesa University is seeking an adjunct instructor of geography. Colorado Mesa University is a state-funded, largely undergraduate institution that emphasizes quality teaching. The standard course in geography at CMU is a 3-credit hour class. The instructor will teach between one and three courses per semester. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching\u00a0introductory-level\u00a0geography courses in human and nature-society geography\u00a0such as World Regional Geography or Human Geography Teaching in other areas of specialization within the geography discipline will be considered, requisite with the candidate\u2019s experience and expertise. The ability to teach quality courses including delivering course content, facilitating student discussions and activities, assessing student learning, and providing timely and responsive communication and feedback to students. Minimum Qualifications Required: Master\u2019s degree in geography or related field. Well versed in geography with the capacity to teach introductory-level geography courses. Experience with basic classroom technology. Ability to teach in all modalities. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates with a PhD in geography or related field will be given preference. Candidates with experience teaching and using GIS in the classroom will be given preference. Candidates that can teach in-person will be given preference. Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. \u200c How to Apply: Applicants should submit a CV with a list of previous courses taught and the contact information for three references. Any questions can be directed to Audrey Lumley-Sapanski, alumley-sapan@coloradomesa.edu. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Psychology_JR100726-1": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Social and Behavioral Sciences department at Colorado Mesa University is seeking an adjunct instructor of psychology. Colorado Mesa University is a state-funded, largely undergraduate institution that emphasizes quality teaching. The standard course in psychology at CMU is a 3-credit hour class. The instructor will teach one course to start, with the potential for future offerings. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching\u00a0introductory-level psychology courses such as\u00a0General Psychology and Human Growth and Development. Teaching in other areas of specialization within the psychology discipline will be considered, requisite with the candidate\u2019s experience and expertise. The ability to teach in-person lecture format, as well as online. The ability to teach quality courses including delivering course content, facilitating student discussions and activities, assessing student learning, and providing timely and responsive communication and feedback to students. Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. \u200c Minimum Qualifications Required: Master\u2019s degree in psychology. Experience teaching introductory-level psychology courses. Experience with basic classroom technology Preferred Qualifications: Candidates that can demonstrate excellence in teaching the required courses for this position will be given preference. Candidates with experience using the Desire 2 Learn (D2L) learning management system will be given preference. Candidates with strong communication skills and demonstrated responsiveness to students will be given preference. DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Jeremy Tost, jtost@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:\u00a0 Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Physics_JR100727": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Physics", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Physics in the Physics Program. This is a full-time, tenure-track position starting the Fall 2027 semester. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. Scholarship in the discipline, involvement with advising, and service to the university, department, and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a0include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach physics courses and labs across introductory through upper-division levels for liberal arts and science majors. Establish a research program in area of expertise with meaningful opportunities for undergraduate physics majors. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Participate in the ongoing assessment and improvement of the physics program and curriculum. Engage in service to the university, department, and profession. Salary: $63,000-$68,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! Minimum Qualifications Required: \u00a0 Ph.D. in physics or a closely related discipline by summer 2027. Effectiveness in teaching and creating a positive learning environment.\u00a0 Enthusiasm for working with and inspiring undergraduate students. Ability and enthusiasm for supervising undergraduate physics and/or astronomy research. Ability to communicate and work collaboratively and collegially with colleagues. Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Enthusiasm for teaching all introductory physics and astronomy classes. Enthusiasm for teaching Electronics for Scientists, Intermediate Laboratory, and/or Advanced Laboratory. Enthusiasm for teaching current upper-division courses and/or developing new courses related to the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. Research interests that diversify the research of current CMU physics faculty. Postdoctoral teaching and/or research experience. \u00a0 How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.\u00a0In addition, please be prepared to upload a:\u00a0 Cover letter CV Statement of teaching interests; listing previous teaching experience and courses, examples of classroom techniques, future approaches for effective teaching, and teaching interests including physics courses offered at CMU. Statement of research interests; listing research interests and experience, potential projects that involve undergraduates, and approximate budget. Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed. If your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.\u00a0Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Names and contact information for three references. \u00a0 Application Deadline:\u00a0 The search closes December 14, 2026.\u00a0 To ensure consideration, complete applications must be received by December 13, 2026, at 11:59 PM Mountain Standard Time. \u00a0 Direct Inquiries Contact:\u00a0 Brian Hosterman, bhosterman@coloradomesa.edu\u200b Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."}}, "rows": {"https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Clinical-Professor-of-Nursing_JR100681": {"school_id": 173, "posting_url": "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Clinical-Professor-of-Nursing_JR100681", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "school of nursing", "area_key_words": "Nursing", "deadline_of_application": "October 15, 2026", "position_start_date": "2026-09-04"}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100682": {"school_id": 173, "posting_url": "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100682", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Medical Office Assisting", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Medical Office Assisting; Medical Assistant program", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-09-04"}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Sociology_JR100667": {"school_id": 173, "posting_url": "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Sociology_JR100667", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Sociology", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Sociology; requisite", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-09-03"}, "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-Master-of-Science-in-Occupational-Therapy_JR100562": {"school_id": 173, "posting_url": "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-Master-of-Science-in-Occupational-Therapy_JR100562", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant or Associate Professor/Clinical Professor